; A region parameter is instantiated ONCE per call, like a type
; variable (docs/memory-model-v2-design.md §2.4). `pair` asks for two
; strings from one region `@r`; `twoRegions` hands it one from `@s` and
; one from `@t`, two regions its own signature keeps apart: AX3063 at
; the call. `oneRegion` passes the same `@s` value twice and is SILENT,
; and `plain` - a caller that names no region at all - passes two
; values from its own region and is silent too, which is MM-RGN-4: a
; program that never writes `@` is the one-region instance.
(:: pair (-> (String @r) (String @r) Int))

(fn (pair a b) 0)

(:: twoRegions (-> (String @s) (String @t) Int))

(fn (twoRegions x y) (pair x y))

(:: oneRegion (-> (String @s) Int))

(fn (oneRegion x) (pair x x))

(:: plain (-> String String Int))

(fn (plain x y) (pair x y))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
